; ..\MCAL364\Mcu\ssc\src\Mcu.c	  2496  **                                                                            **
; ..\MCAL364\Mcu\ssc\src\Mcu.c	  2497  ** Syntax          :  void Mcu_SetMode( const Mcu_ModeType McuMode )          **
; ..\MCAL364\Mcu\ssc\src\Mcu.c	  2498  **                                                                            **
; ..\MCAL364\Mcu\ssc\src\Mcu.c	  2499  ** Description     : This API sets the device to idle, sleep or standby mode. **
; ..\MCAL364\Mcu\ssc\src\Mcu.c	  2500  **                   In Idle mode, the CPU is idle and peripherals are active.**
; ..\MCAL364\Mcu\ssc\src\Mcu.c	  2501  **                   In sleep mode, the CPUs are idle and selected peripherals**
; ..\MCAL364\Mcu\ssc\src\Mcu.c	  2502  **                   are put to sleep and other peripherals work at gated     **
; ..\MCAL364\Mcu\ssc\src\Mcu.c	  2503  **                   clocks. In standby mode, the CPU and all peripherals are **
; ..\MCAL364\Mcu\ssc\src\Mcu.c	  2504  **                   put to sleep. On a wakeup event after idle/sleep, the    **
; ..\MCAL364\Mcu\ssc\src\Mcu.c	  2505  **                   program execution continues from last instruction before **
; ..\MCAL364\Mcu\ssc\src\Mcu.c	  2506  **                   it went to sleep. On a wakeup event after standby, the   **
; ..\MCAL364\Mcu\ssc\src\Mcu.c	  2507  **                   program execution starts from the reset vector.  Please  **
; ..\MCAL364\Mcu\ssc\src\Mcu.c	  2508  **                   refer the HW UM for the pre-conditions to be taken care  **
; ..\MCAL364\Mcu\ssc\src\Mcu.c	  2509  **                   before invoking Mcu_SetMode for the desired mode.        **
; ..\MCAL364\Mcu\ssc\src\Mcu.c	  2510  **                                                                            **
; ..\MCAL364\Mcu\ssc\src\Mcu.c	  2511  ** Service ID      : 0x08                                                     **
